sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Customer
    participant UI as Palermo Web UI
    participant App as Palermo Application
    participant DB as Authoritative Palermo Data
    participant Stripe as Stripe Sandbox
    participant Delivery as Internal Delivery Simulator

    Customer->>UI: Review cart and start checkout
    UI->>App: Submit checkout request
    App->>App: Verify ACTIVE authenticated Customer
    App->>DB: Load cart, variants, prices, customisations, promotion, addresses and delivery method
    DB-->>App: Current authoritative checkout data
    App->>DB: Check current available inventory

    alt Price / availability / promotion / delivery changed
        DB-->>App: Current state differs from submitted checkout
        App-->>UI: Return changed checkout information
        UI-->>Customer: Require review before retry
    else Checkout data remains valid
        DB-->>App: Sufficient available stock
        App->>DB: Atomically create bounded inventory reservation
        DB-->>App: Reservation created
        App->>DB: Create order snapshots and separate payment record using idempotent transaction identity
        DB-->>App: Order ID and payment reference

        App-->>UI: Present provider-controlled payment step
        UI->>Stripe: Customer supplies payment credentials directly
        Stripe-->>UI: Provider payment result
        UI->>App: Return provider result/reference
        App->>Stripe: Verify payment result server-side
        Stripe-->>App: Verified payment status/reference

        alt Payment verified successful
            App->>DB: Record successful payment if not already processed
            App->>DB: Commit reserved inventory exactly once
            App->>DB: Record inventory movement exactly once
            App->>DB: Confirm order and generate invoice exactly once
            App->>Delivery: Create single shipment/tracking workflow
            Delivery-->>App: Tracking reference and initial controlled status
            App->>DB: Persist shipment/tracking record
            App-->>UI: Order confirmed, invoice available, tracking created
            UI-->>Customer: Show order confirmation
        else Payment failed / expired / abandoned
            App->>DB: Record non-successful payment outcome
            App->>DB: Release bounded inventory reservation safely
            App-->>UI: Payment not completed; eligible retry path
            UI-->>Customer: Show failure / retry state
        end
    end

    opt Duplicate checkout request or provider callback
        App->>DB: Resolve persistent transaction identity / existing business outcome
        DB-->>App: Existing order/payment/inventory/invoice result
        App-->>UI: Return existing outcome without duplicate effects
    end
